{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398827-at-what-point-do-you-get-called-a-caitiff","id":1398827,"title":"At what point do you get called a Caitiff?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-25T11:26:29-07:00","id":1398827,"title":"At what point do you get called a Caitiff?","content":"So you arrive in a new city. You are recently embraced and do not know your sire. But if you frenzy you get animal features.<br /> Or as above, but you are hideously ugly and deformed with a zero appearance. Et cetera. Derangement, fugue state in the presence of beauty, limited feeding preference, painful bite, casts no reflection.<br /> <br /> At what point are you obviously a Gangrel etc with an unknown sire, and where do you get called &quot;Caitiff&quot;? Is it if your clan considers it close enough?<br /> <br /> And in reverse, if you are not particularly good with your clan disciplines and don't frenzy that much, but know your Brujah sire, do the other Brujah really care? The Brujah tend to deny that they have a frenzy problem, they are the most varied clan, and they have occasionally adopted Caitiff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T11:42:40-07:00","id":1398831,"title":"","content":"if you know your brujah sire, then you can't be caitiff, unless you're thinblood<br /> <br /> clan curse doesn't make you necessarily part of a clan, they can just be flaws (you can be toreador with no reflection),<br /> <br /> if you haven't been told your clan, then there's a good chance you're caitiff, even if you happen to manifest a clan curse, there's nothing proving that it's a clan curse and not a random flaw<br /> <br /> iirc, your sire can be unknown, but you can't not know your clan, otherwise you're caitiff (unless of course, you've had your memory wiped after being told your clan).<br /> Lasombra seem fine adopting caitiff with an affinity for Obtenebration (which is surprising, but who am I to judge),<br /> I don't know about other clans (setites/baali probably don't care)<br /> <br /> and yeah, Caitiff often masquerade as Brujah, though I doubt most caitiff would be accepted as part of the clan should the truth be revealed (just my opinion though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T13:40:45-07:00","id":1398865,"title":"","content":"You are getting called Caitiff when it is found out, that you are a vampire with no clan bane and so no clan disciples. That can be, if you made it good for yourselves never happen unless someone hires a Tremere to inspect your blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T14:12:51-07:00","id":1398871,"title":"","content":"Game-wise, you are a Caitiff if that's what says your character sheet.<br /> <br /> In-setting, a Caitiff depends widely from the environment.<br /> <br /> - Not knowing you sire doesn't mean you are automatically a Caitiff, 'cause that's what the Gangrel usually do, and most of them end up Gangrel, not Caitiff.<br /> <br /> - On the other end, many Caitiff are born from Brujah, Ventrue and Toreador that Embrace on the spur of the moment, sometime the Childe ends up a proper Kindred, mostly a Caitiff. A Clanbook (I don't remember which, probably the Brujah one) said that being Caitiff or not is about knowing the lore of your Clan.<br /> <br /> - OR you're Caitiff if you can't perfectly point out the whole line of your ancestor, name by name (or so said another Clanbook, probably the Ventrue one)<br /> <br /> - But then, we have Bloodlines, that are born basically from Caitiff that are able to propagate some kind of weirdness (included proprietary Disciplines, of course). These are Caitiff too, until they get enough power to make people afraid of calling them with that name.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, it all comes down to:<br /> If most of Kindred think you're Caitiff, you are a Caitiff, and you have no say in the matter. Until you do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T14:47:38-07:00","id":1398877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398827-at-what-point-do-you-get-called-a-caitiff?p=1398871#post1398871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- On the other end, many Caitiff are born from Brujah, Ventrue and Toreador that Embrace on the spur of the moment, sometime the Childe ends up a proper Kindred, mostly a Caitiff. A Clanbook (I don't remember which, probably the Brujah one) said that being Caitiff or not is about knowing the lore of your Clan.<br /> <br /> - OR you're Caitiff if you can't perfectly point out the whole line of your ancestor, name by name (or so said another Clanbook, probably the Ventrue one)</div> </div> </div> </div>those don't determine if you're caitiff or not,<br /> they're requirements when presenting yourself to the clan and identifying yourself as part of it,<br /> <br /> if you can't tell your lineage, then they'll consider you caitiff (even if you're not)<br /> if you can tell your lineage, then you are identified as part of the clan,<br /> and they can verify later if necessary","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 06-25-2020, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T15:26:12-07:00","id":1398885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398827-at-what-point-do-you-get-called-a-caitiff?p=1398877#post1398877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">those don't determine if you're caitiff or not,<br /> they're requirements when presenting yourself to the clan and identifying yourself as part of it,<br /> <br /> if you can't tell your lineage, then they'll consider you caitiff (even if you're not)<br /> if you can tell your lineage, then you are identified as part of the clan,<br /> and they can verify later if necessary</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's still dependent on the environment.<br /> Out of the character sheet, &quot;Caitiff&quot; is only an word that (like &quot;thin blood&quot;) is used to define the bottom-feeders of the Kindred society.<br /> For some Elders, for example, all the members of the bloodlines are Caitiff.<br /> For others all the thin bloods are Caitiff too (and &quot;thin blood&quot; often depends on your generation, not really if your character is a thin blood).<br /> Kindred aren't required to be fair. If they can leverage on your (lack of) power to have an edge on anything, they'll do.<br /> And if this means calling you a Caitiff because there's any reason to call you that, they'll do it.<br /> It's an elastic concept that reflects the elitism of the setting you are in.<br /> (So you can expect that the exact definition changes between a city and the other)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T17:04:20-07:00","id":1398900,"title":"","content":"I think originally Caitiff was a term used when no other vampire claimed that this vampire was part of their claim. It was truly used for exiled or abandoned childer, or outright outcasts. In these cases though, the vampires are not mechanically different from their clans.<br /> <br /> Later, the term began to be used for mechanical Caitiff that lacked the Clan Weaknesses and XP mechanics of the Clan Disciplines. The former is just a social distinction. The latter is something like learning your child has an atrocious birth defect that will prevent it from ever entering and living in society.<br /> <br /> The term still gets used in both cases so it can be confusing. However, I think the first case is quite clear. In the second case, such childer are declared Caitiff when their sires (or some other &quot;expert&quot; in the clan) makes the determination that they do indeed lack the traits expected of their clan. In that case, it is like a father learning (or at least believing) that their child is actually the child of some other father and their wife had cheated on them. There is probably a time of increasing suspicion until the father finally has (or at least believes to have) proof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T23:32:23-07:00","id":1398953,"title":"","content":"In a social sense you are called Caitiff until your clan is known to the society. Clans are more or less able to tell other clans by their weaknesses, at least the more obvious weaknesses.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical sense, caitiffs don't technically have a clan. They do not suffer from clan weaknesses nor do they gain discipline benefits. Everything comes at an out of clan cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T19:13:11-07:00","id":1399191,"title":"","content":"<u>Ways You Can Wind Up A Caitiff</u><ul><li>You don't know the clan of your ancestors or deny a heritage you do know, and no one else is able to make a good guess at it.</li> <li>A clan admits one of their members embraced you, but they have rejected you and declared you Caitiff.</li> <li>A clan admits one of their members embraced you, but you have rejected them and declared yourself Caitiff.</li> </ul><br /> *Note, that any of the above options work whether you character sheet says &quot;Caitiff&quot; or if it lists an actual clan. Admittedly, it is less likely if you are mechanically a member of certain &quot;visible minority&quot; clans, such as Gangrel and Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> <u>Ways You Wind Up Not A Caitiff</u><ul><li>Your sire (and/or their clan-mates) has clan membership and publicly acknowledges you are a member of the clan. Your sire need not be happy they embraced you, they just need to admit it.</li> <li>Someone with some amount of status, usually a primogen or better, says they know your lineage and vouches for you. This usually makes you a member of their clan, but they might have witnessed another clan embracing you. Bribery is an option.</li> <li>Often the &quot;vouching for&quot; scenario results from a Tremere blood test. Very expensive bribery might be an option.</li> <li>You declare yourself a member of a clan, seem to roughly match what people expect of that clan, and no one in the clan bothers to challenge your claim.</li> <li>You don't declare yourself a member of a clan, but so closely match what people expect of a clan they just assume your are a member of that clan.</li> <li>You declare yourself a member of a bloodline (real or fictitious!), and people in power accept your claim. Remember, the Prince can't just log onto &quot;ObscureBloodlines.com/membership_records&quot; to check your story.</li> </ul><br /> **Note, that any of the above options work whether your character sheet says &quot;Caitiff&quot;, or if it lists an actual clan. Admittedly, some are more likely if you are mechanically a member of certain &quot;visible minority&quot; clans, such as Gangrel and Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T12:22:50-07:00","id":1399350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398827-at-what-point-do-you-get-called-a-caitiff#post1398827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you arrive in a new city. You are recently embraced and do not know your sire. But if you frenzy you get animal features.<br /> Or as above, but you are hideously ugly and deformed with a zero appearance. Et cetera. Derangement, fugue state in the presence of beauty, limited feeding preference, painful bite, casts no reflection.<br /> <br /> At what point are you obviously a Gangrel etc with an unknown sire, and where do you get called &quot;Caitiff&quot;? Is it if your clan considers it close enough?<br /> <br /> And in reverse, if you are not particularly good with your clan disciplines and don't frenzy that much, but know your Brujah sire, do the other Brujah really care? The Brujah tend to deny that they have a frenzy problem, they are the most varied clan, and they have occasionally adopted Caitiff.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Catiff vampire is a lick whose embrace for whatever supernatural reason DID NOT trigger the clan curse placed by Caine on the antediluvians and the specific affinities of those lineages do not manifest into the vampire either.<br /> How do you know someone is a Catiff? Well in some cases it's easy: your Nosferatu sire expects you to change and you do not... he immediately realizes you are Catiff and not Nosferatu, same with Lasombras and mirrors. In most other cases it will take observation from the sire and its peers. They'll notice the curse is not triggered or the fact the fledgling lacks any affinity with the parent clan disciplines. Confirming the embrace &quot;didn't take&quot; can also be done via blood sorcery and some especially attuned sires may even know what happened the moment the embrace has been completed (I reserve this last one mostly for Malkavians...).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T13:53:55-07:00","id":1399659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398827-at-what-point-do-you-get-called-a-caitiff?p=1398831#post1398831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you know your brujah sire, then you can't be caitiff, unless you're thinblood<br /> <br /> clan curse doesn't make you necessarily part of a clan, they can just be flaws (you can be toreador with no reflection).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its a good point about the curses potentially being flaws, but how common is the knowledge about that in-game?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398827-at-what-point-do-you-get-called-a-caitiff?p=1399350#post1399350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Catiff vampire is a lick whose embrace for whatever supernatural reason DID NOT trigger the clan curse placed by Caine on the antediluvians and the specific affinities of those lineages do not manifest into the vampire either.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Caitiff&quot; is both a mechanical game designation and an in-game social class. The two often overlap, but not always.<br /> <br /> In game materials we've seen a Ventrue who never developed a blood preference, got told to leave and never claim Ventrue lineage. A Nosferatu who did not turn ugly but still was allowed to live in the warren. Both of which knew their sires and line. We've got a 5300 years old Caitiff that went head to head with an Antediluvian when they were both fledgelings. There is also the notion that if you find out who your sire is later and can prove it, or the sire confirms, you have a clan. Even though at this point you would have long calcified as someone without clan Disciplines and a clan flaw.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}